{
  "name": "version-bump",
  "source": {
    "folder": "evals/skims/contrived/version-bump",
    "repo": "stockline",
    "kind": "branch"
  },
  "title": "Retry a failed feed fetch before giving up on the run",
  "description": "The supplier's CDN drops a connection a few times a day, and each one has been costing us a whole five-minute cycle plus a page to the on-call. This retries the fetch, twice by default (`FEED_RETRIES`), with a short backoff, and only fails the run once every attempt has failed.\n\nThe fetch now takes its `request` function as a dependency so the retry can be tested without a server. Bumped to 1.5.0 since the retry changes what a transient outage looks like in the logs, and raised the Node floor to 20, which is what every depot runs now and what `undici`'s current release needs.",
  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "6ea9bd0b05de852eccb9ffe2e6d7efdef95d702f",
      "subject": "Retry a failed feed fetch before giving up on the run",
      "body": "Two retries by default, FEED_RETRIES to change it. The fetch takes its\nrequest function as a dependency so the retry is testable. 1.5.0, Node 20."
    }
  ],
